:: StoryTitle
16 Ways To Kill A Vampire At McDonalds


:: StoryData
{
  "ifid": "103F32BA-F72F-48AF-A572-DDC5A1387E8C",
  "format": "Harlowe",
  "format-version": "3.3.9",
  "start": "StartGame_Menu",
  "zoom": 1
}


:: "Follow me." {"position":"2276,1531","size":"100,100"}
She stands. She shuffles her pamphlets into a neat pile and tucks them inside the top garabage bag on her cart.

"What's your name?" I ask, since we're going to be walking together.

"Bess, dear," says Bess.

She's ready to follow me.
(set: $bess_follow to true)

[[Awesome.->Street]]


:: 16 More Ways to Kill a Vampire {"position":"107,1743","size":"100,100"}
(if: $sequence is 0)[It's night. We're standing outside another McDonalds.
(set: $sequence to 1)
This time there's a whole NEST of vampires inside.

Luckily, I have Maggie and Luke with me.

We're pretty good at this shit, and we've got time.

We decide to challenge ourselves by killing every vampire in a different way.


[[Go inside.->16 More Ways to Kill a Vampire]] ](elseif: $sequence is 1)[We encounter the first vampire in the main room.

He's lapping at the neck of a |cash>[dead cashier.](click: ?cash)[

//Poor guy. We were too late to save him, but now we're here to avenge him.//]

The vampire rises and hisses at us.

How do we kill him?
(set: $sequence to 2)

|one>[Attack him with the AED Defibrillator.]
(click: ?one)[(set: $option to 1)(go-to: "16 More Ways to Kill a Vampire")]
|two>[Kill him with silver.]
(click: ?two)[(set: $option to 2)(go-to: "16 More Ways to Kill a Vampire")]
|three>[Kill him with the tears of a virgin.]
(click: ?three)[(set: $option to 3)(go-to: "16 More Ways to Kill a Vampire")] ](elseif: $sequence is 2)[Maggie distracts him with |hand>[hand-to-hand combat.](click: ?hand)[

//Maggie is a lot stronger than I am and wraps her arms in rosary beads, which stops vampires from hitting her full force. That's why she can do this shit and I just get insta-killed. TBH, if you were playing Maggie in this game, it would have been a lot shorter.//]

(if: $option is 1)[I run to the wall and grab the emergency |fib>[AED Defibrillator.](click: ?fib)[

//Fortunately for us, it's real old. One of the 400 joules types that leave third degree burns.//]

Luke slaps the pads on the vamp's back, and I jab the shock button repeatedly.

The defibrillator detects that the vampire is dead, and tries to shock him back to life.

He jitters with electrical current, and eventually catches on fire and burns up.](elseif: $option is 2)[I run to the counter and dig through the cash register.

I find all of the |dimes>[pre-1964 dimes and quarters] in the coin drawer. (click: ?dimes)[

//Before 1964, dimes and quarters contained 90% actual silver. True fact.//

]I hand them to Luke. Luke makes a slingshot out of my hair band and a plastic spoon.

He flings the coins at the vampire. He lands one smack in the vampire's right eye.

The vampire screams as his eye melts out.

Luke melts his face off with more coins.](elseif: $option is 3)[While Maggie fights, I discover a surviving cashier locked in the bathroom, weeping over his Employee of the Month plaque.

I collect some of his tears in a Styrofoam cup.

I splash the vampire with them.

The vampire hisses in pain as the virginally pure tears burn through his flesh and melts him into a slurry of ash and sadness.]

(set: $sequence to 3)
[[Next vampire.->16 More Ways to Kill a Vampire]] ](elseif: $sequence is 3)[We make our way into the kitchen.

Another vampire jumps from her perch on top of the soda machine, trying to ambush us!

We have seconds to react!
(set: $sequence to 4)

|one>[Impale her with a knife!]
(click: ?one)[(set: $option to 1)(go-to: "16 More Ways to Kill a Vampire")]
|two>[Impale her with nails!]
(click: ?two)[(set: $option to 2)(go-to: "16 More Ways to Kill a Vampire")]
|three>[Impale her with a burning red poker!]
(click: ?three)[(set: $option to 3)(go-to: "16 More Ways to Kill a Vampire")] ](elseif: $sequence is 4)[(if: $option is 1)[Maggie whirls around. I blink and her |knives>[knives] are in her hands.(click: ?knives)[

//Maggie's knives are named John and Mina. She's a romantic.//]

She slashes the vampire across the throat, and then stabs up, skewering her heart!

The vampire's last expression is one of |surprise>[surprise] as she poofs into dust.(click: ?surprise)[

//She's probably impressed and honored that Maggie just killed her exactly like Quincey Morris and Jonathan Harker killed Dracula.//] ](elseif: $option is 2)[Luke brings his modified nail gun up to bear.

He shoots the vampire full of nails as she falls.

One in the naval, |chest>[one in each eye], two in the neck, a bunch in the chest.(click: ?chest)[

Luke is a stupid good shot.]

Maggie yanks me out of the way, but the vampire is turning to dust even as she hits the ground where I was standing.](elseif: $option is 3)[For some reason, Maggie has a |poker>[burning red poker.](click: ?poker)[

//I don't ask Maggie about these things.//]

She turns it up and braces it so that the vampire lands on it.

The hot iron burns through the vampire's chest like a blowtorch through butter.

She makes an awful gurgling noise as her lungs are pureed, and then turns to dust.]

(set: $sequence to 5)
[[Next vampire.->16 More Ways to Kill a Vampire]] ](elseif: $sequence is 5)[We prowl into the kitchen proper.

Luke spots |vamp>[another vampire] crouched in the back.(click: ?vamp)[

//They're kind of androgynous looking, and we're not in a situation where we can ask for pronouns, so I'm just going to refer to the vamp as 'them.'

That's what you're suppose to do when you don't know and can't ask? I think?//]
(set: $sequence to 6)

|one>[Remove their heart with a sharpened soup ladle.]
(click: ?one)[(set: $option to 1)(go-to: "16 More Ways to Kill a Vampire")]
|two>[Steak them.]
(click: ?two)[(set: $option to 2)(go-to: "16 More Ways to Kill a Vampire")]
|three>[Lock them in a walk in freezer and let them starve to death.]
(click: ?three)[(set: $option to 3)(go-to: "16 More Ways to Kill a Vampire")] ](elseif: $sequence is 6)[Maggie yells like an amazon and launches herself at the vampire.

She catches them in a tackle, rolls with them on the floor, and |jiu>[brazilian jiu-jitsus] them into a hold.(click: ?jiu)[

//Maggie says that style works on vampires because leverage and mechanical advantage can trump pure physical strength. She's probably right because it looks awesome. It's just a shame a lot of the submission holds don't work because vamps don't need air.//]

(if: $option is 1)[Luke grabs a |ladle>[wooden soup ladle.](click: ?ladle)[

//Quality wooden kitchenware in a McDonalds? How unlikely. That's probably the least believable part of this scenario.//]

He then uses it to scoop the prone vampire's heart right out of their chest.
(set: $feval_count to 1)
It's funky how that works, right? We learned that technique from //Paul Feval's La Ville-Vampire//.](elseif: $option is 2)[Luke grabs a half-made Steak, Egg and Cheese Bagel.

He strips off the egg, cheese, and the bagel, and he slaps it on the vampire's chest.

We have to spend like a minute explaining the pun, but as soon as the vampire gets it, they dissolve into dust.](elseif: $option is 3)[Luke helps her drag the vampire over the the walk-in freezer. They toss them inside, and I slam the door.

Then we put up a sign that says: |donot>["DO NOT ENTER. DEAD INSIDE."](click: ?donot)[

//Because we're all Walking Dead fans.//]

Then Luke drills off the |handle>[door handle.](click: ?handle)[

//Because that's gonna be a lot more effective.//]]

(set: $sequence to 7)
[[Next vampire.->16 More Ways to Kill a Vampire]] ](elseif: $sequence is 7)[A fourth vampire is hanging out in the parking lot behind the McDonalds.

I spot him through the back door. He hasn't noticed us yet.
(set: $sequence to 8)

|one>[Take the ashes of other vampires and throw it at him such that he explodes.]
(click: ?one)[(set: $option to 1)(go-to: "16 More Ways to Kill a Vampire")]
|two>[Trick him into drinking dead blood.]
(click: ?two)[(set: $option to 2)(go-to: "16 More Ways to Kill a Vampire")]
|three>[Throw mustard seeds on the ground.]
(click: ?three)[(set: $option to 3)(go-to: "16 More Ways to Kill a Vampire")] ](elseif: $sequence is 8)[(if: $option is 1)[We sweep up the dust of the other dead vamps.

I take the dustpan outside.

I act all innocent like: "Oh! I am merely a McDonalds employee, taking out some dust."

When the vamp inevitably turns around and tries to eat me, I squeak in surprise and toss the dust in his face.

He immediately explodes.

(if: $feval_count is 1)[This is another gem from //Paul Feval's La Ville-Vampire//.](else:)[It's funky how that works, right? We learned that technique from //Paul Feval's La Ville-Vampire//.]](elseif: $option is 2)[We drag the dead cashier back from the main room.

We clean up the blood, slump him against the wall, and tip his hat down so that it looks like he's sleeping.

Then we hide. I open the back door, letting it slowly creak open. The noise attracts the vampire's attention.

The vampire, who is clearly the runt of the litter 'cause he got stuck sitting in the garage as lookout, looks inside and sees the seemingly sleeping human! He comes over to take a quick, easy drink.

But as anyone who has read Anne Rice's *Interview with a Vampire* knows, the blood of dead humans is actually poisonous to vampires!

He chokes and convulses on the ground.

Then Maggie cuts off his head, because we all learned our lesson from Louis' mistake with Lestat.](elseif: $option is 3)[We can't find any mustard seeds in McDonalds.

So we just scrape a shit-ton of sesame seeds off of hamburger buns.

Once we have about a |bill>[billion], (click: ?bill)[

//Luke: "It's really more like a thousand, Lucy."//

]we open up the back door any toss them out.

The vampire is immediately compelled to start counting them.

That should keep him busy until morning sunlight kills him. We |close>[close the door.](click: ?close)[

//I can still hear him muttering outside: "Fifty three. Fifty four. Fifty five. Wait, that's just lint. Shit. One. Two..."//]]

(set: $sequence to 9)
[[Next vampire.->16 More Ways to Kill a Vampire]] ](elseif: $sequence is 9)[We have to hunt around for the last vampire.

Maggie finally spots her, crouched in the entry tube of the PlayPlace.
(set: $sequence to 10)

|one>[Make a wooden stake spike trap at the bottom of the ball pit and convince her to jump in.]
(click: ?one)[(set: $option to 1)(go-to: "16 More Ways to Kill a Vampire")]
|two>[Find a very loyal McDonalds employee and get him to use his Employee of the Month plaque as a holy object to drive her off.]
(click: ?two)[(set: $option to 2)(go-to: "16 More Ways to Kill a Vampire")]
|three>[Give her a bouquet of roses.]
(click: ?three)[(set: $option to 3)(go-to: "16 More Ways to Kill a Vampire")]
|four>[Destroy her with a shard of the true cross.]
(click: ?four)[(set: $option to 4)(go-to: "16 More Ways to Kill a Vampire")] ](elseif: $sequence is 10)[(if: $option is 1)[Luke gets a bunch of stakes out of the car and makes a trap under the ball bit.

It takes forever, but he is CRAZY pleased with himself when it's done, so it's worth it.

Maggie chases the vamp through the PlayPlace with a crucifix, until the leech flees down a slide, lands in the ball pit, and impales herself.

Luke is just twittering with DIY-flavored glee.](elseif: $option is 2)[I locate a surviving McDonalds employee huddled in the bathroom, crouching protectively over his Employee of the Month placard.

I convince him that only he can banish these monsters from his place of work, using his deep faith in the McDonalds corporation.

We march over to the the PlayPlace. The employee holds his plaque over his head and screams at the vampire about how it has violated company policy and is no longer welcome as a guest in this restaurant.

The vampire spontaneously combusts.

Whoa.](elseif: $option is 3)[Vampires hate plants that symbolize new life.

Good examples: holly, hawthorn, or roses.

I nip out to buy a bouquet of roses from a street vendor.

Luke charges her with the romantic nosegay, but she retreats into the PlayPlace.

Maggie ends up chasing her through the tubes likea tiny blonde monkey.

The vampire gets cornered in one of those transparent plastic bubbles and we watch Maggie thrash her with the boquet.

She dies in a flurry of rose petals and ash.](elseif: $option is 4)[In between killing the other vampires, I snagged an assembled happy meal for a snack.

And wouldn't you know it, my happy meal prize was a shard of the true cross.

All I have to do is wave it in the vampire's direction, and the vampire dies.

This is going to make our job a LOT easier.]

(set: $sequence to 11)
[[Next vampire.->16 More Ways to Kill a Vampire]] ](elseif: $sequence is 11)[Having killed all the |vamp>[vampires] (click: ?vamp)[

//in up to 16 different ways!//

]Maggie, Luke and I exchange high-fives.

Then we go eat at Arby's.

No one wants McDonalds.

Not for a while.


[[The End!->Unlockables]] ]


:: A bucket. {"position":"3122,1962","size":"100,100"}
(if: $inv_bucket_contains is not "")[Unfortunately, the bucket is already full of something!

I'll need to use something else, or go pour this out.


|pour>[Pour it out in one of the kitchen sinks.]
(click: ?pour)[(set: $inv_bucket_contains to "")(go-to: "A bucket.")]
[[Use something else.->Splash vampire with sizzling oil.]] ](if: $inv_bucket_fixed is false)[I quietly move a french fry basket out of the way and fill my empty bucket with boiling oil.

Unfortunately there's a crack in it, so the oil leaks out.


[[Damn.->Splash vampire with sizzling oil.]] ](else:)[I quietly move a french fry basket out of the way and fill my empty bucket with boiling oil.

Feeling downright medieval, I sneak up on the vampire and pour boiling oil down his back.
(set: $vampire_state to "oily")
[[He screams.->vampire notice kitchen]] ]


:: A pamphlet. {"position":"3273,1961","size":"100,100"}
I quietly move a french fry basket out of the way.

I curl the pamphlet and start shoveling up oil and flicking it at the vampire.

The laminate quickly starts wilting under the heat.

The vampire also notices that I'm splashing him with hot oil.
(set: $vampire_state to "slightly oily")
[[He snarls and turns towards me.->vampire notice kitchen]] 



:: A salad. {"position":"907,812","size":"100,100"}
I am not getting a McDonalds salad. McDonalds salads are for |sad_veg>[sad vegetarians].(click: ?sad_veg)[

They aren't sad because they're vegetarians. Vegetarians rock. They're sad because they have inconsiderate friends who make them go to McDonalds so that they have to eat McDonalds salads.] 


[[Order something else.->Order]] 


