:: Fascinating Vampire Facts {"position":"249,1603","size":"100,100"}
(if: $sequence is 0)[**Fascinating Vampire Facts**
//How to Kill Vampires: Basics//
(set: $sequence to 1)
- Stakes.

- Beheading.

- Sunlight.

- Fire.

- Holy Water/Holy Objects.

- Shooting them with a special magic gun.

- Stabbing them with a special sword.


[[More Facts->Fascinating Vampire Facts]] ](elseif: $sequence is 1)[**Fascinating Vampire Facts**
//How to Kill Vampires: Advanced//
(set: $sequence to 2)
- Prevent them from ritually marrying and devouring one maiden each year.

- Get them preemptively in their graves by laying |necks>[scythes] across their necks.(click: ?necks)[

	//They'll slice off their own heads as they rise for the night.//]

- Lure them onto the roof with a |cow>[cowbell]. Then shoot them.(click: ?cow)[

	//They'll think there's a cow they can mess with. Vampires love messing with cows.//]

- Wait until they go to their secret vampire city to have their heart wound up by an |evil>[evil priest.](click: ?evil)[

//Go to said evil city at 13 o'clock, remove their heart with a sharpened soup ladle, and then burn the heart and throw the ashes at other vampires so they EXPLODE.//]


[[More Facts->Fascinating Vampire Facts]] ](elseif: $sequence is 2)[**Fascinating Vampire Facts**
//Vampire Disposal//
(set: $sequence to 3)
Sometimes in addition to slaying a vampire, you have to deal with its corpse.

Vampires have a habit of coming back from being killed. To prevent this, you should:

...cut off the limbs...

...and then shove bricks or garlic into the mouth...

...and then burn everything...

...and then scatter the ashes at a crossroads...

...and sometimes watch for the soul-bearing moth that pops out of a vampire's mouth when it's burning...

...and nail that moth to a tree with a silver or iron nail.


[[More Facts->Fascinating Vampire Facts]] ](elseif: $sequence is 3)[**Fascinating Vampire Facts**
//Stuff Vampires Do Other Than Drink Your Blood//
(set: $sequence to 4)
- Mess with your cows.

- Eat your corn pudding.

- Meet in cemeteries and at crossroads to plan evil vampire shennanagins.

- Kill their family, hang around for seven years, and then leave town to get a fresh start somewhere else with a new, not-dead family.

- Turn into many many many |animals>[animals.](click: ?animals)[

//Pike, roosters, dogs, cats, butterflies, moths, horses, snakes, really whatever.//]

- Mesmerize you with their gaze.

- Be really strong.


[[More Facts->Fascinating Vampire Facts]] ](elseif: $sequence is 4)[**Fascinating Vampire Facts**
//Stuff Vampires Do Other Than Drink Your Blood, Part 2//
(set: $sequence to 6)
- Make dogs freak out.

- Or, alternatively, make dogs shut up.

- Have glowing eyes.

- Have kids who either become great vampire hunters or have no bones.

- Heal all their wounds when the moonlight hits them.

- Steal your hair to become pretty and young again.

- Try to get married MANY MANY TIMES to cure themselves of vampirism.

- Cause droughts and mess with the weather.


[[More Facts->Fascinating Vampire Facts]] ](elseif: $sequence is 6)[**Fascinating Vampire Facts**
//Non-Fatal Weaknesses//
(set: $sequence to 7)
- They get all pissy about any sort of threshold and need to be invited to cross them.

- They |smell>[smell awful.](click: ?smell)[

//Sometimes to the point of KILLING people with their stank.//]

- They cannot appreciate music.

- They cast no |mirror>[reflection.](click: ?mirror)[

//They also throw no shadow, spoil all photographs taken of them, and painters cannot draw them, instead drawing a skeleton or something.//]

- Their power ends at the |crowing>[crowing of the cock.](click: ?crowing)[

//Sometimes even if the cock is crowing in the middle of the night.//]

- They have to tell their life's story to their paramours.


[[More Facts->Fascinating Vampire Facts]] ](elseif: $sequence is 7)[**Fascinating Vampire Facts**
//Non-Fatal Weaknesses, Part 2//
(set: $sequence to 8)
- They have to always use some variant of their |real>[real name.](click: ?real)[

//Thus, Alucard.//]

- Virgins riding unblemished stallions can locate their graves.

- Water just flat out rejects them and they get spat out on shore somewhere.

- They need to sleep in specific types of soil.

- They have certain times when they are and are not powerful.

- They hate the smell of garlic, green nut shells, juniper, perfume, and cow dung.


[[Yet More Facts->Fascinating Vampire Facts]] ](elseif: $sequence is 8)[**Fascinating Vampire Facts**
//How To Become a Vampire//
(set: $sequence to 9)
- Get bit by another vampire.

- Be a total dick who dies.

- Commit suicide.

- Get buried without things you like.

- Have an animal jump over your corpse.

- Have a shadow fall upon your corpse.

- Have your idiot husband makes a supernatural pact to get you back after you die.

- Become one of the 13 disciples of the devil magicians that run the secret school of necromancy known as |Scholomance>[the Scholomance.](click: ?Scholomance)[

//This is Dracula's actual origin story.//]

- Have somebody [[steal your shadow.]]


[[More Facts->Fascinating Vampire Facts]] ](elseif: $sequence is 9)[**Fascinating Vampire Facts**
//Miscellanious Facts//
(set: $sequence to 10)
- Knives, hot pokers, nails, and skewers sometimes also work instead of or in addition to wooden stakes.

- In Russian folklore, there's a lot of "vampire killing" cures that are basically just "cart the vampire to the next village and let those suckers deal with it."

- Sometimes Russians would also just throw their vampires in lakes.

- If you don't drive the stake in with one blow, it sometimes doesn't work.

- Sometimes stakes don't work if the vampire is super in love with somebody and want to visit them.

- |people>[People born on a Saturday] are great at killing vampires, and can summon small magical black dogs to hunt them.(click: ?people)[

//They are called Sabbatari.//]

- Sometimes you can feed people heart ashes to |keep>[keep them from being vampires.](click: ?keep)[

//...or to cure them of |con>[consumption.](click: ?con)[

WARNING: This fact is not actually in the least true.]//]


[[More Facts->Fascinating Vampire Facts]] ](elseif: $sequence is 10)[**Fascinating Vampire Facts**
//That is All the Vampire Facts//
(set: $sequence to 11)
All credit for this section goes to *Leah Davydov*.

She researches vampires professionally. She researched and wrote |every>[everything here.](click: ?every)[

//She is also a Sabbatari.//]

All of these are 100% things that people have written and believed about vampires.


//Sources://
Dracula
Clarimonde
La Dame Pale
La Vampire
Varney the Vampire
Carmilla
The Mysterious Stranger
The Family of the Vourdalak
Paul Feval
La Ville-Vampire
Le Captaine Vampire
Montague Summers
Anne Rice
Folklore


