:: Talk To Cashier {"position":"1026,1062","size":"100,100"}
(if: $cashier_statement is "")["Hey," I whisper conspiratorially.

"Hi!" she says, not picking up on the whisper theme. "Are you feeling better?"

"Sort of. You know that guy in that booth over there?"

"Yes?"


|vampire>["He's a vampire."]

|badvibe>["I'm getting a bad vibe from him."] ](elseif: $cashier_statement is "vampire")[She blinks at me a few times. 

"You know. Toothy? Anemic? Tans easily?"

"Um."

"Twilight has lied to you. They're not cuddly."

"Um."

"Has he ordered anything? I bet he hasn't. You know why?"

"Um."

"He eats blood."

"I'm really not allowed to talk to customers about...other customers."

"Well I sure don't want to get you in trouble. I just want to stop him from murdering and eating you."

"...do you want to order something?"


|vampire2>[Continue] ](elseif: $cashier_statement is "vampire2")[Well that was kind of satisfying. I'm usually not that direct, since people tend to think I'm crazy.

Case in point: how the cashier is looking at me now.

And maybe I'll get to say 'I told you so' to her corpse.

I hope not.


[[Order food.->Order]]

[[Go back to my booth.->Main Room]] ](elseif: $cashier_statement is "badvibe")["Really?" she says. "He seemed pretty nice to me. But if he does anything inappropriate, just let me know. I'll ask him to leave."

Now THAT would be useful. Vampires can't go places if they're not invited. All restaurants have a universal-invitation-aura that mean they can come and go, but if a cashier rescinded his invitation? He'd have to get right out.


|eye>["Would you keep an eye on him?"]

|whats_in>["What's inappropriate?"]

|said_inap>["He said something inappropriate to me."]

|tripped>["He tripped me."]

|vampire>["He's a vampire."] ](elseif: $cashier_statement is "whats_in")["You know," she says, waving a hand. "Talking or doing something inappropriate."

Well that cleared it right up. I think I know what she means though.


|eye>["Would you keep an eye on him?"]

|said_inap>["He said something inappropriate to me."]

|tripped>["He tripped me."]

|vampire>["He's a vampire."] ](elseif: $cashier_statement is "eye")["Would you keep an eye on him?" I ask. "He hasn't done anything, but it would make me feel better."

"Sure!" she says, perking up at the opportunity to be useful.

Very new to the food service industry, this one.

"Thanks," I say.
(set: $cashier_alert to true)

[[Order food.->Order]]

[[Go back to my booth.->Main Room]] ](elseif: $cashier_statement is "tripped")["You know when I fell before?" I say, lowering my voice.

This time she gets it, and lowers her voice with me: "Yeah?"

"I didn't want to say it at the time, but he tripped me."

"Oh my god. Really?"

"Yeah. Stuck his leg out as I was going by."

"That's awful! That's completely inappropriate. Just a second."


[[Continue->tripped_throwout]] ](elseif: $cashier_statement is "said_inap")[(if: $dump_vamp is true)["He said something inappropriate to me," I tell her.

"Oh dear," she says. "What?"

"He came over and flirted with me for like a minute, then called me a bitch when I wouldn't leave with him."

"//Seriously?//"

"Yeah."

"That's just...yuck."

The cashier chews her lip for a moment.

"My manager wouldn't like it, but he's not here right now, and that's majorly skeezy. Just a second."


[[Continue->tripped_throwout]]  ](else:)["He said something inappropriate to me," I tell her.

"But you haven't talked at all," she points out.

I pause. Then slowly nod.

"Okay. That's fair." If I'm going to lie to her, apparently I have to be less transparent.

She frowns at me. "Do you want to order something?"


[[Order food.->Order]]

[[Go back to my booth.->Main Room]] ] ]


