:: luke ending {"position":"2371,1127","size":"100,100"}
(if: $sequence is 0)[CHICKA-BLAST
(set: $sequence to 1)(set: $ChickaBlast to true)
Goes [[Luke's musket.->luke ending]] ](elseif: $sequence is 1)[Normally, guns don't do much against vampires.

However, Luke inherited his gun from his great-grandfather. It was blessed by a priest, a rabbi, a pandit, a monk and basically anyone else with a lick of faith Luke can get to lay hands on it.

When we pass through towns he always tries to convince the local priest-equivalent to do something to his firearm. He collects blessings like some people collect pokemon. He's had the best luck in Texas.

(set: $sequence to 2)
[[Continue->luke ending]] ](elseif: $sequence is 2)[Anyway, the shot catches the vampire in the back.
(set: $sequence to 3)
The musket ball explodes out of |chest>[his chest](click: ?chest)[ (missing me by a narrow but acceptable margin)].

Golden curls of holy power burn glitteringly and dissolve undead flesh until the bullet hole is more like a cannon hole.


[[Continue->luke ending]] ](elseif: $sequence is 3)[The vampire crumples to the ground. We both watch it for a second.

Slowly, it starts to disintegrate into dust. Luke breathes a sigh of relief.

"Thank god," he says. "I'm not up to disposing of another body."

"Yeah," I agree, dabbing at the bite mark on my neck with my fingertips to keep it from dripping onto my camisole.
(set: $sequence to 4)

[[Continue->luke ending]] ](elseif: $sequence is 4)["Yeah," he repeats.

He looks at me, then glances away.

"What?" I ask.

"Are we...still fighting? I mean, does this, you calling me, mean we're not fighting anymore?"


|fighting>["We're still fighting."]
(click: ?fighting)[(set: $sequence to 6)(go-to: "luke ending")]
|not_fighting>["We're not fighting."]
(click: ?not_fighting)[(set: $sequence to 9)(go-to: "luke ending")]
|what_think>["What do you think?"]
(click: ?what_think)[(set: $sequence to 5)(go-to: "luke ending")] ](elseif: $sequence is 5)[His eyes widen and he looks considerably more intimidated by the question than he was by the vampire.

He struggles to figure out an answer and I decide to stop being an immature bitch and just tell him.


|fighting>["We're still fighting."]
(click: ?fighting)[(set: $sequence to 6)(go-to: "luke ending")]
|not_fighting>["We're not fighting."]
(click: ?not_fighting)[(set: $sequence to 9)(go-to: "luke ending")] ](elseif: $sequence is 6)["//Yeah// we're still in a fight," I tell him, crossing my arms. "Unless you think you can listen to me without picking apart every fucking thing I say."

"I don't pick apart everything you say," Luke says as he starts to pick apart what I just said. "That is a complete overstatement. You say lots of things that I don't pick apart."

"You are literally doing it right now," I tell him.

"That's because you said something not true!" He swings his musket into the priming position and starts to agitatedly reload it. "If you just said what you meant..."

"You mean if I was just perfectly logical and calm and never made any mistakes in the //middle// of a //fight//," I throw back at him. "I don't SAY exactly what I mean. NO ONE says exactly what they mean. Especially not when they're in a //fight//."
(set: $sequence to 7)

[[Continue->luke ending]] ](elseif: $sequence is 7)["So you're allowed to just not make sense." Luke is ramrodding gunpowder into the muzzle of his gun very forcefully. "So what, am I supposed to read your mind?"

"No you're supposed to ask goddamn clarifying questions and cut me slack," I tell him.

"Cut you slack." He is not making eye contact with me and it is driving me a little crazy. "Right. Like you're doing for me right now."

"DO NOT FUCKING TURN THIS AROUND ON ME," I yell. "CAN YOU JUST HEAR WHAT I AM SAYING?!"

This goes on for a while.

Fortunately the vampire is dead.
(set: $sequence to 8)

[[Continue->luke ending]] ](elseif: $sequence is 8)[Luke and I scream at each other in the alley for a while.

Mostly I scream. Motherfucker stonewalls me, which is just as bad.

Finally he breaks down and starts yelling (read--ACTUALLY engaging with me).

And then he starts crying and then that stops me yelling.

And then we actually talk.

Finally.

[[Happy ending.->Endings]] ](elseif: $sequence is 9)["No we're not," I rub the back of my neck.

I am still kind of pissed at him, but I don't want to get into it in an McDonalds alley.

"Okay good," there is profound relief in his voice and he gives me a little smile as he swings his musket into the priming position and starts to reload it.

I like his little smiles.

[[Good night, all told.->death ending]] ]


:: maggie ending {"position":"2375,996","size":"100,100"}
