:: toilet {"position":"2925,881","size":"100,100"}
I'm good, thanks.


[[Stop up the toilet.]]

[[Continue->Bathroom]]


:: toilet end {"position":"3092,727","size":"100,100"}
(if: $sequence is 0)[I flush the toilet a few more times. |water>[Water](click-replace: ?water)[*Mercifully //clear// water*] collects in the bowl and spills out onto the floor.

I open up the back of the toilet. I know just enough about the mechanics of these things to wedge the chain in such a way that it's perpetually flushing.
(set: $sequence to 1)
I leave the scene of my crime. A steady stream of toilet water follows me out the door [[back into the main room.->toilet end]] ](elseif: $sequence is 1)[I casually stroll out of the bathroom, leaving the door ajar, and sit in my booth.
(set: $sequence to 2)
It takes a minute for the cashier to notice what's happening. When she does she makes a soft distressed noise and heads towards the bathroom.

The vampire perks up, excited that his prey seems to be isolating herself. He tries to follow her.

He reaches the stream of water and just stops.


[[Continue->toilet end]] ](elseif: $sequence is 2)[It's funny. He looks like a mime. A really good mime doing an invisible wall routine. It takes him a second to figure out what's going on.
(set: $sequence to 3)
Then he looks down, and sees the running water.

A rivulet of it arcs toward him and he has to skip back.

His expression is like: "Really? REALLY?!"


[[Continue->toilet end]] ](elseif: $sequence is 3)[Five minutes pass.
(set: $sequence to 4)
The cashier is still in the bathroom, making upset confused noises. I don't think plumbing falls within her repertoire, which makes me feel simultaneously relieved and sorry for her.

The water spreads to the point where the vampire is standing on a tiny island of dry linoleum on the far end of the room.

I'm sitting on the table of my booth.

I consider making faces at him.


[[Continue->toilet end]] ](elseif: $sequence is 4)[A couple more minutes, a couple more liters of water, and the vampire is forced to the door.

(if: $bucket_trap is true)[ [[He opens it.->heads towards the door.]] ](else:)[He slams it behind him and stalks off into the night.

I pump my fist in the air!

Then I go into the bathroom to help the cashier fix what I did to her toilet.
(set: $RunningWater to true)

[[This was weird, but it worked.->drive off ending]] ]]


:: tripped_throwout {"position":"1026,1212","size":"100,100"}
Adorable cashier marches out from behind the counter and over to the vampire.

The vampire looks surprised that his intended meal is confronting him directly.

He's even more surprised when she orders him out of the restaurant.

It's fun to watch him double march to the door, glaring back in irritation as ancient rites of hospitality force his feet forward.

He looks like he's trying out for Monty Python. I can't help but smile.

(set: $Uninvited to true)
[[Continue->heads towards the door.]]


